;
; brig runs passt as root inside pasta's user namespace. With the SELinux
; policy of passt 0^20261002, passt_t may not use the setfcap capability in
; that namespace, which passt needs to sandbox itself, so no VM can start
; ("Couldn't write to /proc/N/uid_map: Operation not permitted").
;
; The rule sits in an optional block, so that the module still loads, and
; takes effect once passt's module is present, if passt-selinux is not
; installed yet or is removed later: passt_t is defined by that module.
(optional brig_passt
    (allow passt_t self (cap_userns (setfcap))))
